// Structural admission of total duality to the existing discrete-category
// classifier. Object truncation and groupoidality are preserved by reversal.
// This is a declared classifier closure, not a derivation of new inverse data
// for Core_incl_func from the presently qualified dual-functor beta rules.
symbol discrete_total_op [C : Cat] (C0 : τ (IsDiscreteCat C))
  : τ (IsDiscreteCat (TotalOp_cat C));

// Ordinary categories remain ordinary after total duality. Hom reverses its
// endpoints and is itself totally dualized; its discrete profile is retained.
symbol one_cat_total_op [C : Cat] (C1 : τ (IsNCat (cat_succ cat_zero) C))
  : τ (IsNCat (cat_succ cat_zero) (TotalOp_cat C))
≔ λ x : τ (Obj C), λ y : τ (Obj C),
    @discrete_total_op (Hom_cat C y x) (C1 y x);
